earlier versions.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Latest Documentation on Godot Engine\n\n### Issue description\n\nThere is one specific issue within the documentation, due to the unfortunate oversight of the individual who wrote [this](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_packedfloat64array.html#class-packedfloat64array-method-to-byte-array) specific section. You see, in this quote:\n> [PackedByteArray](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_packedbytearray.html#class-packedbytearray) to_byte_array() const [🔗](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_packedfloat64array.html#class-packedfloat64array-method-to-byte-array)\n>\n> Returns a copy of the data converted to a [PackedByteArray](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_packedbytearray.html#class-packedbytearray), where each element have been encoded as 8 bytes.\n>\n> The size of the new array will be float64_array.size() * 8.\n\nThere has been a grave grammatical error within this statement:\n\n> where each element have been encoded as 8 bytes.\n\nIn this statement, \"have\" is not appropriate. The correct word should be \"has\".\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nGo to this [link](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_packedfloat64array.html#class-packedfloat64array-method-to-byte-array). The issue is self-evident.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nRefer to reproduction steps above.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u